{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DqVBo5NxctUJ8oWgshyE1k","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found Kirk True's mailing list discussion about **KIP-1324: Support client configuration observability**. Here are the relevant files:\\\\n\\\\n## Kirk True's Initial Discussion Post\\\\n**File:** `/store/events/2026/04/23/mail-6c643315a34fcdb22f25b861-715ae5bb.md`\\\\n- **Date:** April 23, 2026\\\\n- **List:** dev@kafka.apache.org\\\\n- Kirk True initiated the discussion by posting a link to the KIP-1324 page on the Kafka Confluence wiki with an invitation for community feedback.\\\\n\\\\n## Related JIRA Issue Creation\\\\n**File:** `/store/events/2026/04/23/mail-808bc6785589a2f7f1be1aa5-bf083309.md`\\\\n- **Date:** April 23, 2026\\\\n- **Issue:** KAFKA-20525 (Support client configuration observability)\\\\n- This notification indicates the creation of the corresponding JIRA issue that describes the feature: a new RPC called `PushConfig` through which clients send their configuration to brokers, and a new `ClientConfigPolicy` interface for brokers to process these RPCs.\\\\n\\\\n## Discussion Responses\\\\n**File:** `/store/events/2026/04/28/mail-97891a965c325ea00d480c20-332c2e0b.md`\\\\n- **From:** Hector Geraldino (Bloomberg)\\\\n- **Date:** April 28, 2026\\\\n- Raised questions about enforcing configuration policies, overwriting client configurations, and extending KIP-714 metrics\\\\n\\\\n**File:** `/store/events/2026/04/28/mail-ff97e55ba5d2cf756212a8d2-c767502b.md`\\\\n- **From:** Andrew Schofield\\\\n- **Date:** April 28, 2026\\\\n- Provided detailed technical feedback with 11 points (AS1-AS11) covering topics like profile concept clarity, configuration lists, error codes, timing considerations, and connection performance impacts.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"events/2026/01/08/mail-00ea238280fabc66d3475e44-5671594d.md\\\",\